{"reference":"Psalms 134","book":"Psalms","chapter":134,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Psalms Leading to Psalm 134","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 134 stands at the end of a sequence that includes communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and songs oriented toward worship. This wider setting is disputed, but it places the chapter’s call to bless the LORD within a larger collection shaped by both loss and worship.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_134_b55c4d2c45599877c29e62be"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}